# How to install python3, per distro family — read by python_install_hint().
# isopod's core needs no python; the agent commands (claude-code, codex) do, to
# read a release manifest and check the download's SHA-256 before it goes into a
# box. `isopod remap` also prefers it when git-filter-repo is absent.
#
# Whitespace-separated: <family> then the rest of the line is the command.
# Families come from distro_family(); 'macos' and 'unknown' are the fallbacks.
#
# family   command
debian     sudo apt install -y python3
fedora     sudo dnf install -y python3
arch       sudo pacman -S --needed python
gentoo     sudo emerge --ask dev-lang/python
suse       sudo zypper install -y python3
alpine     sudo apk add python3
macos      xcode-select --install   (or: brew install python)
unknown    install python3 with your package manager
